  "craters_missing": [],
  "description": "A patch centred on each benchmark crater is the query. It ranks every regular 3.84 km grid patch from the other regions. A grid patch counts as a hit when its window fully contains another benchmark crater's rim (|dx| and |dy| at most 1.92 km minus half the crater diameter); grid patches within 5 km of a crater that do not contain it are left out. Positives per crater: Barringer (Meteor Crater) 1, New Quebec (Pingualuit) 0, Lonar 1, Roter Kamm 0, Tenoumer 1, Tswaing (formerly Pretoria Saltpan) 4, Wolfe Creek 4. Craters with no positive (rim wider than the window allows at the grid offset) still act as queries.",
  "index": "Index: all valid Earth grid patches (land-cover masks off).",
  "combined_note": "The Earth-to-Earth combined row uses sigma 0.163, at which the terrain term is close to zero for most crater pairs, so it tracks the embedding. The app's Moon targets use sigma 0.46-0.93, where the terrain term carries real weight; the Moon-target row uses their median (0.71) and is the closer match to the app's ranker.",
  "hard_negative_note": "Hard negatives: only the non-crater patches (more than 5 km from any benchmark crater) of the other crater tiles, on average 6,495 per query. These are non-crater terrain from the same landscapes as the other benchmark craters, so a ranker that only recognised the landscape type would score close to chance (0.5) here.",
  "weights_note": "Why the app still weights terrain features 60%: they carry the slope, relief and roughness values that operations planning needs, and the 0.6/0.4 split was set before this benchmark existed. Changing it now, after seeing these results, would tune the method on its own test set. V3 reports how the top 10 changes under other splits.",
  "finding": "At 60 m the 20 interpretable terrain features alone recognise 1-3 km craters only weakly (AUC 0.63, about the same as relief alone at 0.63, random 0.55); the learned image embedding does much better (AUC 0.98, another crater in the top 10 for 86% of queries). Against hard negatives (non-crater patches from the other crater tiles) the embedding's AUC is 0.98 and the features' 0.54. With the Moon-target sigma the combined score reaches AUC 0.88. The app uses both: feature values to explain a match in physical units, and the embedding to rank landform shape.",
  "revision_note": "An earlier version of this test also used the crater-centred patches as the relevant candidates. The embedding then ranked another crater first for every query (mean reciprocal rank 1.00, AUC 0.979), an artefact of exact centring that a real search never has. Candidates are now regular grid patches only; the positive rule above was fixed from geometry before this run.",
  "masked": {
   "description": "Same test on the masked search index used by the app (1 query crater survives the masks; removed by the land-cover masks: Barringer (Meteor Crater), Lonar, New Quebec (Pingualuit), Tenoumer, Tswaing (formerly Pretoria Saltpan), Wolfe Creek). With fewer than three query craters these numbers are not meaningful; they are shown for completeness only.",
